# What this plugin is, for the index in README.md and for whoever installs
# it alone. One key per line, a key repeated for each line of a message;
# ./xymon-plugin at the repository's top installs it from the lines below.
name: xymonapi-mcp
version: 0.1.1
summary: an MCP server that gives an AI client read-only tools over the Xymon API
server-short: the MCP server, beside the API for /ask
tools-short: the MCP server for your AI tools
writes: ~/.claude.json (xymonapi-mcp register)
writes: ~/.codex/config.toml (xymonapi-mcp register)
requires: xymonapi >= 0.1.0 (its client beside it; the API over the network, XYMONAPI_URL), python >= 3.9
manual: xymonapi-mcp.1

# How ./xymon-plugin installs it: see xymonapi's PLUGIN file.
server-needs: xymonapi
tools-needs: xymonapi
server-files: server.py xymonapi-mcp.sh
server-manual: xymonapi-mcp.1
uninstalled: Uninstalled xymonapi-mcp. Kept: xymonapi.
tools-files: server.py xymonapi-mcp.sh
tools-manual: xymonapi-mcp.1
command: xymonapi-mcp xymonapi-mcp.sh
executable: xymonapi-mcp.sh
installed-tools: Next, once: xymonapi-mcp register URL -- the API's address as this machine reaches it, or, on the Xymon
installed-tools:   server, unix: and the API's local socket, which install --server prints (xymonapi(8), XYMONAPI_SOCKET). It runs xymonapi-connect, then registers the server with Claude Code and Codex.
uninstalled-tools: Uninstalled xymonapi-mcp. What register did besides, to undo by hand:
uninstalled-tools:   claude mcp remove --scope user xymon; codex mcp remove xymon
uninstalled-tools:   revoke this machine's token: curl -X DELETE -u USER https://SERVER/xymon/api/v1/tokens/$(hostname -s)
uninstalled-tools:   rm ~/.config/xymonapi/xymon.token ~/.config/xymonapi/xymon.url
